# visual parity artifacts (not source)
.altitude/visual-parity/
# visual-compare holds throwaway local-vs-prod captures, EXCEPT the brand
# distinctiveness harness and its committed artifact, which are review
# evidence for .altitude/BRANDS.md. `/*` (not `/`) so the negations below can
# re-include — git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded.
.altitude/visual-compare/*
!.altitude/visual-compare/harness/
!.altitude/visual-compare/brands.dark.png
# The scoped `<al-theme brand>` proof — four brands in ONE document with one
# `:root`, which the four-iframe brands.dark.png harness cannot express.
!.altitude/visual-compare/brands.scoped.png
# The same proof through the REACT wrapper, captured from the @southleft/al-react
# Storybook's `Foundations/Theme` -> `Brand` story. Its own artifact because
# `<ALTheme>` reaches the attributes by a different route than lit-html does
# (see libs/al-react/src/components/Theme/Theme.tsx) and can regress alone.
!.altitude/visual-compare/brands.react.png
.altitude/visual-parity-before/
.altitude/visual-parity-after/
.altitude/icon-check/
# AI-readiness. The two DIGESTS are tracked: run-probe.mjs:84,87 and
# run-judge.mjs:182-183 name them as the ground truth an agent (and the judge)
# must verify tag/attribute/slot/event/token claims against, and AGENTS.md
# points agents at them. A fresh clone with no digest silently degrades every
# agent to source-tree guessing. They are regenerated by
# `pnpm --filter @southleft/al-web-components build` and drift-gated in CI
# (.github/workflows/v2-checks.yml, job `cem-and-contracts`).
# Per-run OUTPUT is transient and stays ignored — attempts/*.json + run.json
# + judge-*.json + report.json can be multi-megabyte and are reproducible
# from a fresh run. `/*` (not `/`) so the negation below can re-include —
# git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded (same
# trick as the visual-compare block above).
.altitude/ai-readiness/runs/*
# The curated BASELINE is the one exception: build-scorecard.mjs distills a
# completed (or honestly-partial) run into a small stable-schema
# scorecard.json — see scripts/ai-readiness/schemas/scorecard.schema.json.
# That's tracked so the delta loop the README describes has a committed
# reference point instead of only commit-message folklore.
!.altitude/ai-readiness/runs/baseline/

# Playwright MCP scratch
.playwright-mcp/


# Astro generated types cache
**/.astro/

# >>> monday-morning:mm >>>
# .mm/ is local-only in git BY DESIGN — team sharing happens via the Monday
# Morning cloud workspace (Settings → Team visibility). Do not force-add past this.
.mm/
# <<< monday-morning:mm <<<
# .claude/ is TRACKED so skills, agents, commands and CLAUDE.md survive a clone.
# Only the machine-local parts stay ignored:
# NOTE: .gitignore has no trailing comments - a comment on a pattern line becomes
# part of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing.
# live git worktrees + full repo snapshots; never commit
/.claude/worktrees/
# personal overrides
/.claude/settings.local.json
# regenerated locally
/.claude/.mm-manifest.json
.mcp.json

# Secrets. The AI Theme addon (.storybook/ai-theme) reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# from a local .env during `storybook dev`; production reads it from the
# Cloudflare Pages environment. Never commit either.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars

# Cloudflare Workers/Pages local dev state — `pnpm dlx wrangler pages dev`
# (used to verify libs/altitude-mcp/src/worker.mjs + functions/api/mcp.js
# under real workerd, see libs/altitude-mcp/README.md "Hosted endpoint")
# writes this in the CWD it's run from. Local-only, machine-specific.
.wrangler/

# Figma sync exports (agent-mediated loop — see .altitude/FIGMA-SYNC.md).
# The parity MANIFEST is carved out: it is durable sync state (which Figma set
# each component maps to + last-confirmed-sync hashes), same category as the
# tracked .altitude/migration.json — without it a fresh clone reads every
# component as "missing in Figma" in Storybook's parity badges.
# (`/*` not `/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded)
.altitude/figma-sync/*
!.altitude/figma-sync/parity-manifest.json
# Parity is MULTI-PROJECT (.altitude/ds-projects.json): every design system other
# than the default keeps its manifest in its own subdirectory. Re-admit those
# directories, re-ignore their contents, then carve out each manifest — the same
# three-step dance as above, one level deeper. `ops/` and `tmp/` are re-admitted
# by the first line but hold no parity-manifest.json, so nothing else leaks in.
!.altitude/figma-sync/*/
.altitude/figma-sync/*/*
!.altitude/figma-sync/*/parity-manifest.json

# NOTE: generated parity REPORTS need no rule here. The emitter writes them all
# into `libs/al-web-components/dist/` (`parity.json` for the default project,
# `parity.<projectId>.json` for the others), which that package's own
# .gitignore:7 already covers. Only the parity MANIFESTS above are tracked.

# Scratch artifacts that kept landing at the repo root. These are agent/verify
# working files and one-off screenshots, never source. Named explicitly rather
# than by a blanket `*.png` so intentional image assets elsewhere still commit.
/.claude-verify-tmp/
/.mm-backup-*/
/*.png
/*-spec.json
**/_*_backup.txt

# V8 coverage output from `pnpm run test:unit:coverage`. Regenerated on every
# run; the only durable artifact is the floor in
# `.altitude/baselines/coverage.json`, which IS tracked.
/coverage/
/tmp-shots

# The story fixture is a build artifact — rebuilt by `pnpm run build:story-fixture`
# whenever the a11y sweep runs. Only its source is durable.
libs/al-web-components/story-fixture/dist/

# Pagefind writes its index into the built docs output, which is already ignored.
# Listed explicitly so a stray index next to source is never committed.
**/pagefind/

# Copied from apps/southleft/public/logos at build time by
# apps/docs/scripts/copy-brand-assets.mjs. One source of truth: the owning app.
apps/docs/public/logos/
